# Changelog

All notable changes to Zuqongsoft Music are recorded here.

The format follows [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/), and versions follow
[Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).

## [Unreleased]

## [1.0.3] - 2026-10-30

### Added

- GitHub Actions release workflow (`.github/workflows/release.yml`), triggered by `v*` tags and manual runs only:
  - checks that every Python file compiles, that the tag matches `version_info.txt`, and that release notes exist for the version;
  - builds with Nuitka and Inno Setup on Windows;
  - creates a draft GitHub Release with the installer, its SHA-256 checksum and the version's release notes.
- `tools/release_notes.py`: extracts one version's section of `RELEASE_NOTES.md` and fills in the checksum.
- Issue forms for bug reports and feature requests; blank issues turned off; links to troubleshooting and private security reporting.
- `.gitattributes`: CRLF line endings for Windows scripts on every checkout.

### Changed

- README: automated builds, release steps and issue templates.

### Fixed

- Version details: the app and installer report the correct version.

## [1.0.2] - 2026-10-22

### Added

- Nuitka build (`build_nuitka.bat`): compiles the app to native code into the same `dist/ZuqongsoftMusic` folder as the PyInstaller build; copies `libmpv-2.dll`; excludes unused optional libraries (Pillow, NumPy, Tkinter).
- `build_installer.bat /nuitka`, and build switches (`/nuitka`, `/skipbuild`, `/nopause`) that work in any order.
- Code signing pipeline (`tools/sign.ps1`):
  - signs the app, unsigned bundled libraries, the installer and the uninstaller, with RFC 3161 timestamps and fallback servers;
  - identities: certificate-store thumbprint (USB tokens, cloud HSMs, test certificates), PFX file, or Microsoft Artifact Signing;
  - configured through `signing.env` or `SIGN_*` environment variables.
- Signing check before signed installer builds: identity, installed certificate, private key, expiry and `signtool`.
- `tools/make_test_cert.ps1` for testing signing with a self-signed certificate.
- SHA-256 checksum file written next to each installer.

### Changed

- Release builds are compiled with Nuitka.
- Build scripts only call PowerShell when signing is configured, so unsigned builds are unaffected by script execution policies.
- Shared `BUNDLED` check (`app/__init__.py`) recognises both PyInstaller and Nuitka builds. It's used to find libmpv next to the executable, to relaunch after installing libmpv, and to register the AppUserModelID in installed copies.
- `.gitignore` excludes `signing.env`, certificate files and checksums.
- README: Nuitka build, installer switches, code signing, PowerShell tips and troubleshooting.

## [1.0.0] - 2026-10-21

First public release.

### Added

#### Library

- Background, incremental folder scanner (mutagen tags; embedded or folder cover art) backed by SQLite with automatic schema migrations.
- Songs table with sortable columns; default order artist → album → disc → track number.
- Album grid with asynchronously loaded cover art; search across title, artist and album.
- Playlists with M3U import and export; drag a folder onto the window to add it.
- Genre tags read and stored for automatic EQ rules.

#### Playback

- mpv (libmpv) audio engine with gapless playback, and automatic fallback to Qt Multimedia when libmpv is missing.
- In-app download of libmpv, with a clear message listing every folder that was searched.
- Up Next queue: Play next / Add to queue, drag to reorder, remove; queued songs survive shuffle and new albums or playlists.
- Session restore: the last queue and track reload, paused at the saved position.
- DJ mode:
  - crossfades of 1–12 s using two decks and equal-power curves;
  - silent intros and outros trimmed from scan data;
  - fades on play, pause and skip, with 1.2 s blends when changing songs;
  - gapless consecutive album tracks.
- Song Radio and Autoplay, scored from artist, genre, co-listening history, ratings, play and skip counts and recency, with artist variety.
- Sleep timer (15–90 minutes or end of song) with fade-out.

#### Lyrics and karaoke

- Synced lyrics view with smooth auto-scroll and click-to-seek; free scrolling pauses auto-follow.
- Lyrics sources: `.lrc` beside the song, embedded tags (ID3 SYLT/USLT, Vorbis, MP4, WMA), then LRCLIB online with result caching and two-week retry for misses.
- Lyrics editor:
  - import `.lrc` or `.txt`;
  - tap-to-sync (F8) with exact playback time;
  - ±0.1 s nudge and timestamp removal;
  - save as `.lrc` with title/artist/album tags, falling back to the app's data folder for read-only music folders.
- Karaoke: centre-vocal reduction that keeps bass below 150 Hz, and ±6 semitone key change that keeps the tempo.

#### Equalizer and Studio

- 10-band equalizer:
  - pre-amp, limiter and 13 presets;
  - user presets, live response curve and 0.1 dB steps;
  - Frequency (Hz) / Gain (dB) table import and export.
- Separate EQ profiles per output device; new devices inherit the current curve.
- Studio EQ, parametric with up to 16 bands:
  - band types: peak, low and high shelf, low and high cut, notch;
  - drag-to-edit graph that draws the real RBJ biquad response;
  - AutoEq / Equalizer APO / REW parametric import and export, or export as a 10-band table;
  - A/B comparison at matched loudness, band solo (button or Ctrl+drag sweep);
  - undo/redo and snapshots A–D;
  - third-octave spectrum analyser (bit-identical output), EBU R128 LUFS meter (M/S/I/true peak), L/R level and stereo correlation meters;
  - target curves (Harman over-ear and in-ear approximations, warm, bright, custom CSV) and headphone measurement overlay with predicted result.
- Studio tools:
  - tone tilt;
  - stereo width, balance, mono, L/R swap and polarity;
  - compressor and 3-band multiband compressor;
  - de-esser, bass enhancer and exciter;
  - crossfeed;
  - convolution with WAV impulse responses.
- Automatic EQ rules per genre, album or song, managed from a song's context menu or the Equalizer tab.

#### Sound

- Volume boost to 200% as a filter before the limiter (no clipping), with a one-time hearing warning on headphones and Bluetooth, and reset to 100% on start.
- "Make quiet songs louder" dynamic levelling, and ReplayGain.
- Library loudness levelling: background EBU R128 scan at about 150× real time, with selectable targets (−14 / −16 / −18 / −23 LUFS).
- Exclusive mode (WASAPI), high-quality resampling, speaker layout (automatic / stereo / surround), and a "What's playing now" source and output format panel with bit-perfect detection.
- Speakers and surround: stereo → 5.1 upmix, virtual surround for headphones (SOFA head model with one-click MIT KEMAR download), 2.1 Linkwitz–Riley crossover, per-speaker delays.
- Output device picker with Bluetooth and hands-free detection, hot-plug handling, pause on disconnect and switch on connect.
- Shortcut to Windows Loudness Equalization settings.

#### Stats

- Play and skip tracking based on listened time, star ratings, and listening history.
- Six smart playlists, and "Your year in music" with totals, top songs, artists and albums, monthly chart and biggest day.

#### Interface

- Material 3 design generated from seed colours:
  - 10 presets in light and dark, a custom colour, or follow the system;
  - Match album art (Material You-style colour extraction);
  - Appearance window with live previews;
  - the Windows 11 title bar follows the theme.
- Responsive wide / medium / compact layouts with animated transitions; columns hide as the table narrows.
- Now-playing pane with Playing / Lyrics / Up Next tabs.
- Full-screen Now Playing: animated cover-colour background, synced lyrics, spectrum, auto-hiding controls and karaoke mode.
- Mini player and tray icon, with an option to keep playing in the tray.
- App icon (water-droplet note) with a simplified small-size variant.

#### Windows integration

- System media overlay (SMTC) with metadata and cover art.
- Global hotkeys (Ctrl+Alt+Space / ← / → / ↑ / ↓) and media keys.
- App identity (AppUserModelID) for installed copies, so the overlay, notifications and taskbar show the app's own name and icon.

#### Build and distribution

- PyInstaller spec with version information.
- `build.bat` and `build.sh`, with file checks, virtual-environment repair, libmpv download and output verification.
- Inno Setup installer:
  - per-user install without administrator rights, or all users;
  - Start Menu and optional desktop shortcuts;
  - clean upgrades;
  - uninstaller that optionally removes user data.
- README with setup, build, usage, shortcuts, troubleshooting and licence notes.

